Let's Encrypt's newer roots, ISRG Root YE (ECDSA) and Root YR (RSA). Today
adsb.lol and adsb.im still send chains that end in a cross-sign by ISRG Root
X2 or X1, but once a server stops sending the cross-sign, the last
certificate's issuer is one of these.
Root YE, SHA-256 e14ffcad5b0025731006caa43a121a22d8e9700f4fb9cf852f02a708aa5d5666
(same key as the copy api.adsb.lol serves, cross-signed by ISRG Root X2).
